we dont need to check since its directed so no going back to parent

but if we use undirected logic and graph is like

0 --> 1 <-- 2

we might call it cyclic, since 1 is visited twice and parent is not same

so we maintain inRecurrsion array that keeps track of each element visited in current recurrsion

we check in visited array first, if it is not visited then go ahead and see if we find cycle
 
but if visited then check if we visited it in same recurrsion in inrecurrsion array

if we did then cycle is there, otherwise we move to next neighbhour

code : 

class Solution {
    
    public boolean dfs(int u, ArrayList<ArrayList<Integer>> adj, boolean[] v, boolean[] i){
        v[u] = true;
        i[u] = true;
        
        for(int x : adj.get(u)){
            if(!v[x] && dfs(x, adj, v, i)) return true;
            else if(i[x]) return true;
        }
        
        i[u] = false;
        return false;
    }
    
    public boolean isCyclic(int V, ArrayList<ArrayList<Integer>> adj) {
        boolean[] v = new boolean[adj.size()];
        boolean[] i = new boolean[adj.size()];
        
        for(int u = 0; u < adj.size(); u++) if(!v[u] && dfs(u, adj, v, i)) return true;
        return false;
    }
}
